  "content": {
    "id": "p22-q22-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "A circle of radius $\\sqrt{3}$ is inscribed in a regular hexagon below.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [
      {
        "id": "p22-q22-diagram",
        "role": "question",
        "format": "tikz",
        "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"geometry\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[],\"reference\":\"source page 22, p22-q22-diagram\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=10mm,line width=0.8pt]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\draw[black] (2,0)--(1,{sqrt(3)})--(-1,{sqrt(3)})--(-2,0)--(-1,{-sqrt(3)})--(1,{-sqrt(3)})--cycle;\n\\draw[black] (0,0) circle[radius={sqrt(3)}];\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
        "src": null,
        "widthMm": 42,
        "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
        "overlayOf": null,
        "transparent": false,
        "axes": null,
        "spec": {
          "sourcePage": 22,
          "sourceRegion": "Question 22, upper left column",
          "description": "Regular hexagon with horizontal top and bottom sides and a circle tangent to all six sides. Source pink fill is omitted under the unshaded house convention; no measurements or construction lines are added.",
          "mathematics": "Circumradius 2 and inradius √3 in the internal coordinate model; the student figure has no numerical labels.",
          "answerVisibility": "Only the supplied hexagon and inscribed circle are visible."
        },
        "derived": false,
        "reviewStatus": "needs-review"
      }
    ],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p22-q22-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the area of the hexagon. Hint: divide the hexagon into equilateral triangles.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$6\\sqrt{3}$ square units.\n\nDivide the hexagon into six equilateral triangles.",
          "worked": "Join the centre to the six vertices. Each equilateral triangle has height $\\sqrt{3}$. Let its side length be $s$. Bisecting it gives\n$$\\begin{align*}\\left(\\frac{s}{2}\\right)^2+3&=s^2\\\\\\frac{3s^2}{4}&=3\\\\s^2&=4\\\\s&=2.\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore,\n$$\\begin{align*}A_{\\text{hexagon}}&=6\\times\\frac12\\times2\\times\\sqrt{3}\\\\A_{\\text{hexagon}}&=6\\sqrt{3}\\text{ square units}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 78
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q22-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the area of the circle.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3\\pi$ square units.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}A_{\\text{circle}}&=\\pi r^2\\\\A_{\\text{circle}}&=\\pi(\\sqrt{3})^2\\\\A_{\\text{circle}}&=3\\pi\\text{ square units}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q22-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Explain how this shows $\\pi<4$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\pi<2\\sqrt{3}<4$.\n\nThe circle has less area than the enclosing hexagon.",
          "worked": "The hexagon contains the circle and has additional area outside it. Hence\n$$\\begin{align*}3\\pi&<6\\sqrt{3}\\\\\\pi&<2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $\\sqrt{3}<2$, we have $2\\sqrt{3}<4$. Therefore $\\pi<4$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      }
    ]
  },
